// Hot reload counter - version 3, deliberately broken migration hook
//
// BT-3540 (ADR 0123 Phase 5): same shapeVersion: 3 / field shape as
// hot_counter_v3.bt, but migrateFromV2: unconditionally raises — exercising
// ADR 0123 §3's suspend-on-failure path end-to-end: a live instance
// reloaded against this module is left suspended (not resumed on the old
// shape, not killed), its state stays intact and inspectable, and a later
// `:load` of the corrected hot_counter_v3.bt re-suspends (idempotent) and
// resumes it.
//
// `self error:` runs fine here even though migrateFromVN: hooks execute via
// `local_call/3` with `self` bound to `nil` (ADR 0123 §2 — no class-process
// context): `error:` is an ordinary instance-side Object method, and `nil`
// (UndefinedObject) inherits it like any other object.

Actor subclass: HotCounter
  shapeVersion: 3
  state: value = 0
  state: step = 5
  state: bonus = 0

  class migrateFromV2: old :: Dictionary -> Dictionary =>
    self error: "BT-3540 e2e: migrateFromV2: deliberately broken"

  increment => self.value := self.value + 10

  getValue => ^self.value

  getStep => ^self.step

  getBonus => ^self.bonus
